# A1: the AUDITED INTERLEAVED attach and exactness run on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-levern-audit (the audited best arm, chunked prefill on, QWEN_FAST_LEVER_N=1 at the 0.5 prefill share, QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_AUDIT=1).
# The same tests as A0c. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) the engaged markers - "lever N installed on", "lever N: chunked prefill kept for qwen3_5 (budget=262144 threshold=0)",
# "lever N route installed: route=1", "lever N route warmed before the packed traces: steps=3" - and the route warm BEFORE Metal's unsafe-allocation warning; (2) per split prompt the route ledger (c2_smoke_check
# levern_problems): one "lever N route" line per step, each start the previous end, every non-final end a multiple of 2,048, the decode slot written by the final step alone, no program compiled by a step;
# (3) the alternation visible in the "lever N step" lines whenever decoders and a partial coexist (levern_equal_busy); (4) every answer's hash, token count and finish equal to A0c's, and every digest line
# (GDN slot, logits, KV pages) per prompt length equal to A0c's: python scripts/ci/levern_compare.py --control <A0c smoke log> --levern <A1 smoke log> --control-container <A0c container log> --levern-container
# <A1 container log> exits 0. ANY difference is NO-GO: the claim is that a split prefill equals the whole one bit for bit. Record the program-cache counts of the route lines and the memory ledger's free DRAM.
# Duration (estimate): 2.5 h (the KV digests read the whole pool to the host, about a minute each). Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/lever-n four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lever-n and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lever-n-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/lever-n commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lever-n-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-levern-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy,levern_equal_long
